          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On June 5, 1955, at 8:55 PM, three witnesses in Cavaillon observed for 20 seconds in the direction of the west side of the Luberon mountain range a red-hot rectangular light in the sky. Initially stationary, the phenomenon then moved very quickly, changing shape (from a crescent to a ball) and heading towards the east. It shrank and then disappeared. Astronomical verification eliminated the Moon as a possibility. The hypothesis of an airplane was abandoned. The GEIPAN classified this case as C due to lack of information and corroboration.",
